      <li>The <em>Codex Regius</em> (GkS 2365 4°), c. 1270 CE. — primary manuscript; <em>Grímnismál</em> stanza 20.</li>
      <li>Larrington, C. (1996). <em>The Poetic Edda</em> (trans.). Oxford University Press. p. 56. — translation.</li>
      <li>Faulkes, A. (ed., 1987). <em>Edda</em>. Everyman. p. 33. — Prose Edda; name etymology note.</li>
      <li>Simek, R. (1993). <em>Dictionary of Northern Mythology</em>. D.S. Brewer. p. 160. — name meanings.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="qa-claim-note"><strong class="claim-lore">[lore]</strong> named cultural/historical source</p>
  </section>

